---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Accessibility" description="AquaSense's accessibility approach, implemented features, known limitations, and testing checklist.">
  <PageHero index="A" eyebrow="Accessibility" title="Access is part of the build." lead="This site aims to make a technical story usable across devices, input methods, reading preferences, and visual conditions." />
  <div class="section-shell access-shell">
    <section class="prose" data-reveal>
      <p class="eyebrow">Approach</p>
      <h2>Designed toward WCAG 2.2 AA.</h2>
      <p>The project uses semantic HTML, a consistent heading structure, keyboard-operable controls, visible focus states, a skip link, text alternatives, responsive layouts, and reduced-motion support.</p>
      <p>Charts include a text description and an expandable data table. Result states use labels and symbols alongside color. The light and dark themes are both designed to maintain readable contrast.</p>
    </section>
    <section data-reveal>
      <div class="check-grid">
        <article><span>01</span><h3>Keyboard</h3><p>Navigation, theme controls, accordions, tabs, filters, and the simulator can be operated without a pointer.</p></article>
        <article><span>02</span><h3>Structure</h3><p>Landmarks, page titles, heading order, labels, captions, and ARIA relationships provide a meaningful reading sequence.</p></article>
        <article><span>03</span><h3>Perception</h3><p>Color is redundant, text can reflow, focus is visible, and animation respects <code>prefers-reduced-motion</code>.</p></article>
        <article><span>04</span><h3>Data</h3><p>Interactive charts update their accessible descriptions and expose the same values in an HTML table.</p></article>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="prose" data-reveal>
      <p class="eyebrow">Known limitations</p>
      <h2>Accessibility is tested, not declared once.</h2>
      <p>This portfolio build has been reviewed at common responsive widths and with automated checks. A production project should additionally include testing with multiple screen readers, browser zoom to 400%, voice control, representative users, translated content, and real low-bandwidth devices.</p>
      <div class="notice">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 3 2.8 20h18.4L12 3Zm0 6v5m0 3h.01" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
        <p>If you encounter a barrier, open an issue in the <a href="https://github.com/ZhiyuanHuang02/AquaSense-demo/issues">GitHub repository</a> with the page, browser, assistive technology, and expected behavior.</p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .access-shell { display: grid; gap: clamp(5rem, 10vw, 9rem); }
  .access-shell .prose { margin-inline: auto; }
  .check-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: var(--radius); overflow: hidden; }
  .check-grid article { min-height: 280px; padding: 2rem; background: var(--paper-raised); }
  .check-grid article:nth-child(odd) { border-right: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .check-grid article:nth-child(n+3) { border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .check-grid span { color: var(--coral); font: .7rem 'DM Mono', monospace; }
  .check-grid h3 { margin: 3rem 0 1rem; }
  .check-grid p { color: var(--ink-soft); }
  code { padding: .15rem .3rem; background: var(--aqua-pale); border-radius: .25rem; font-family: 'DM Mono', monospace; font-size: .8em; }
  @media (max-width: 650px) {
    .check-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .check-grid article:nth-child(odd) { border-right: 0; }
    .check-grid article:nth-child(n+2) { border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
  }
</style>
